Chapter: Capability

Section: Kernel Capability Bits

  cap-console : Integer = 0
  cap-concurrent : Integer = 3
  cap-console-read : Integer = 4
  cap-console-write : Integer = 5
  cap-filesystem-read : Integer = 6
  cap-filesystem-write : Integer = 7
  cap-network-read : Integer = 8
  cap-network-write : Integer = 9
  cap-block-device : Integer = 10
  cap-ipc : Integer = 11
  cap-process-create : Integer = 12
  cap-capability-admin : Integer = 14
  cap-identity : Integer = 15
  cap-device : Integer = 16
  cap-gpu-compute : Integer = 17
  cap-gpu-memory : Integer = 18
  cap-camera : Integer = 19
  cap-microphone : Integer = 20
  cap-location : Integer = 21
  cap-sensors : Integer = 22
  cap-display : Integer = 23
  cap-flash : Integer = 24
  cap-audio : Integer = 25
  cap-process : Integer = 26
  cap-gpio : Integer = 27
  cap-uart : Integer = 28
  cap-spi : Integer = 29
  cap-i2c : Integer = 1
  cap-adc : Integer = 2
  cap-power : Integer = 13
  cap-rng : Integer = 30

Section: Directions

  cap-dir-read : Integer = 0
  cap-dir-write : Integer = 1
  cap-dir-readwrite : Integer = 2

Section: The Table

 `[Process]` guards host authority, and `run-process` in particular is
 arbitrary command execution, which is why it takes a bit of its own
 rather than borrowing Concurrent's `cap-process-create`, the bare-metal
 spawn authority.

  CapSpec = record {
   cs-name : Text,
   cs-id : Integer,
   cs-base-bit : Integer,
   cs-read-bit : Integer,
   cs-write-bit : Integer,
   cs-extra-bits : List Integer
  }

  capability-table : List CapSpec
  capability-table = [
   CapSpec {
     cs-name = "Console",
     cs-id = 0,
     cs-base-bit = cap-console,
     cs-read-bit = cap-console-read,
     cs-write-bit = cap-console-write,
     cs-extra-bits = []
   },
   CapSpec {
     cs-name = "FileSystem",
     cs-id = 1,
     cs-base-bit = 0 - 1,
     cs-read-bit = cap-filesystem-read,
     cs-write-bit = cap-filesystem-write,
     cs-extra-bits = []
   },
   CapSpec {
     cs-name = "Network",
     cs-id = 2,
     cs-base-bit = 0 - 1,
     cs-read-bit = cap-network-read,
     cs-write-bit = cap-network-write,
     cs-extra-bits = []
   },
   CapSpec {
     cs-name = "Concurrent",
     cs-id = 3,
     cs-base-bit = cap-concurrent,
     cs-read-bit = 0 - 1,
     cs-write-bit = 0 - 1,
     cs-extra-bits = [cap-ipc, cap-process-create]
   },
   CapSpec {
     cs-name = "Device",
     cs-id = 4,
     cs-base-bit = cap-block-device,
     cs-read-bit = 0 - 1,
